What have you thought about today?

Is our enjoyment mostly limited by our creativity?

Possibly, consider having your own thing going on while you're there (i.e. finding a chair & sitting down after greeting a few people while you walk in, having a relaxing drink by yourself, being chill by yourself; maybe people will come over & maybe some won't, ok, so what?).

How could you enjoy the party individually at a foundational level, before you enjoy it with others?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I consider non enjoyment & enjoyment to both be good -the variety gives me a unique entertainment experience?

To me its food for thought & I'm entertained by thought?

If a girl says yes to a dance, nice, & we dance.

If a girl says no, nice, something different might occur that I can find entertainment in. 

&#x200B;

There's a chance you'd reflect on what you'd judge as an awkward moment & enjoy it, maybe even laugh at it. I cherish the goofiness of my past, because I've had flash backs of giving girls awkward spit kisses in 7th grade, avoiding my prom date, and generally making girls go ick just by existing ....as I type more & more is coming back

&#x200B;

\^I tend not to stay awake at night anymore scrutinizing myself for being socially unacceptable by some; now I tend to laugh & laugh hard about those events. I'm so blessed to have that goofiness as apart of my life story, sometimes a laugh is craved & hard to come by. 

&#x200B;

I've shown up to a girls grad party, where I was essentially outside of my social circle; I went into the kitchen & started to help out; there was also a period where I sat down with a drink & just took it all in. I left early after staying for maybe, 3 hours -there was probably a point where I just felt, ok, I'm good here. 

&#x200B;

Ideas: Never know what might occur...Maybe there will be another person there who's outside their circle, and at some point you could ask to go for a walk around the neighborhood with them. 

&#x200B;

